<title>INDIA: Hindalco 97/98 aluminium turnover down.</title>
<headline>Hindalco 97/98 aluminium turnover down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's largest private aluminium maker, HIndalco INdustries Ltd., said on Wednesday it expected its aluminium turnover in financial 1997/98 (April-March to drop to 388,000 tonnes from 389,000 tonnes the previous year.  </p>
<p>Hindalco Chairman Kumar Mangalam Birla made the remarks at the company's annual general meeting.</p>
<p>The firm forecast metal turnover in 1997/98 at 208,000 tonnes as compared to 167,000 tonnes the previous year.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
